WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:12.350
Larry P. Arnn: The Constitution and current
politics. The Constitution is 227-28 years

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:16.330
old this year.
Richard: Our fathers set forth on this continent

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:22.259
a new nation conceived in liberty.
Larry P. Arnn: This is the great constitutional

00:00:22.259 --> 00:00:25.300
crisis that the conservative movement was
born to face.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:30.790
Larry Kudlow: This is a fight worth preserving.
Not only because of its track record, it's

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:35.750
a fight worth preserving for the generations
ahead of us—for the unborn. That's why this

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:43.670
is so important. I'm a great believer that
democracies breed Free Market Capitalism.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:52.150
Life, yes. Liberty, yes. Pursuit of happiness
means you are free to fail or succeed, and

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:58.159
in so doing you will produce great things
that nobody believed possible. I don't ever,

00:00:58.159 --> 00:01:03.800
ever want to lose that freedom.
Heather: The lesson from the last 20 years

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:11.820
of immigration policy is that lawlessness
breeds more lawlessness. If someone cannot

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:17.860
be removed for illegal entry, then there is
no more immigration law.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:23.420
Larry P. Arnn: Our government, by consent,
is justified by the fact that we can talk

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:28.710
to each other. We have human souls which is
a reflection of the divine soul.

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:33.770
Martha: When the cold war ended, the United
States government got out of the business

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:37.159
of representing the United States to the rest
of the world.

00:01:37.159 --> 00:01:42.399
Larry Kudlow: If we want to be optimistic
about the great country of ours and the great

00:01:42.399 --> 00:01:53.519
economy of ours, we, you and I, are going
to have to fight like hell to preserve it.

